# Mount Hosmer Avalanche Digital Twin (Stage 3) -- environment template
# Copy to `.env` (same folder) and edit. Every value below is optional; the
# commented default is what the application uses when the variable is absent.
#
# Stage 3 serves entirely from the one-time bake under runtime\baked\. The running
# service needs NO source data and no database -- most of the old knobs are gone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data locations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read-only source data (LiDAR DEM/DSM, land cover, terrain fallback, metadata).
# Used ONLY by `python -m app.bake`; never read at runtime. The app never writes here.
# Windows default: ..\DATA\mount_hosmer_data -- a sibling of this project folder.
AVALANCHE_DATA_ROOT=D:\school\capstone\Avalanche\DATA\mount_hosmer_data
# Linux / Docker:
# AVALANCHE_DATA_ROOT=/data/mount_hosmer_data

# Everything the application generates -- above all runtime\baked\. Must NOT be
# inside AVALANCHE_DATA_ROOT.
# AVALANCHE_RUNTIME_ROOT=./runtime

# Pre-1.0 names. Still honoured, but AVALANCHE_* takes precedence. The compiled
# launcher sets these.
# MOUNT_HOSMER_DATA_ROOT=
# MOUNT_HOSMER_RUNTIME_ROOT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# development | production
# APP_ENV=development

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API. Use localhost (not
# 127.0.0.1) for the Next dev server -- Next 16 blocks dev resources cross-origin.
# AVALANCHE_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bake grid (metres) -- read only by `python -m app.bake`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terrain grid. Built from the 1 m BC LiDAR by area-averaging, so lowering this
# raises fidelity and cost quadratically. 5 m over the ~12x12 km AOI is
# 2400x2400 px per layer. Do not raise it to 30 m: that discards the LiDAR.
# AVALANCHE_TERRAIN_RESOLUTION_M=5

# Environmental layers (land cover, forest mask). Coarser than terrain on purpose:
# the source data is 10 m, so a finer grid would only interpolate.
# AVALANCHE_ENVIRONMENTAL_RESOLUTION_M=10

# Gap-fill grid, used only where LiDAR is missing (Copernicus GLO-30 is 30 m).
# AVALANCHE_FALLBACK_RESOLUTION_M=30

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local AI assistant (Ollama) -- optional, fully offline
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assistant talks to an Ollama server. Without it, the /api/assistant/*
# routes return a clean 503 and the rest of the app is unaffected. To enable:
#   ollama serve  &&  ollama pull llama3.1:8b
# AVALANCHE_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# AVALANCHE_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# How long to wait on a model turn. Raise it when Ollama is remote (e.g. reached
# through a tunnel) -- an 8B model on a laptop is not fast.
# AVALANCHE_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_S=120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service split -- only relevant when running as separate services
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# See docs/deployment.md. Unset (the default) means ONE process serving
# everything: `uvicorn app.main:app`, the .exe launcher, and docker compose.
#
# Setting this switches the assistant from calling the assessment model
# in-process to calling a remote assess service over HTTP. It is the single
# variable that separates the two deployment shapes. The assistant still never
# computes a hazard number itself either way.
# AVALANCHE_ASSESS_URL=http://assess.internal:8080
# AVALANCHE_ASSESS_TIMEOUT_S=90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is INLINED at BUILD time, not read at run time.
# Changing either value means rebuilding the frontend, not restarting it. Both
# must be the URL the BROWSER can reach -- not one the container can reach.
#
#   unset          -> http://localhost:8000 (local development)
#   "" or "/"      -> SAME ORIGIN: emit relative paths like /api/assess. This is
#                     the shape used behind a single load balancer that
#                     path-routes to all three services -- and it is why the
#                     deployed app needs no CORS configuration at all.
#   https://host   -> that absolute origin
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# The assistant service, when it is deployed separately. Unset falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, so the single-process shape needs nothing here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSISTANT_BASE_URL=
